      "text": "— Startup founders often enter a company with a huge ego and an assumption that they know a lot more than everyone else. I suggest doing the opposite. Assume everyone else is smarter than you. Spend most of your time asking questions, hearing people out, and studying the business. Then, once you have a clear picture of what’s going on, share your (informed) pespective."
